# Normalize text files to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true in its *system* config, so a
# Windows clone would otherwise land CRLF in the working tree while the index
# stays LF. Biome formats to LF and checks the working tree, so every file then
# fails `pnpm lint`. Pinning eol=lf here overrides the inherited setting for
# this repo without asking each contributor to reconfigure their git.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Already detected as binary by content; declared so nothing can mangle them.
*.icns binary
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
